import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
O=Path(__file__).parent
old=[r for r in json.loads((O/'propulsion-body-ablation.json').read_text())['validation'] if r['variant']=='rpm_9x45'];new=[r for r in json.loads((O/'conservative-joint-body-ablation.json').read_text())['validation'] if r['variant']=='rpm_9x45']
fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(9,4));x=np.arange(6)
ax.bar(x-.18,[r['bank_rmse_deg'] for r in old],.36,label='Original joint torque');ax.bar(x+.18,[r['bank_rmse_deg'] for r in new],.36,label='Potential-gradient joint torque');ax.set_xticks(x,['HR 447','HR 450','HR 508','TL 326','TL 402','TL 3387']);ax.set_ylabel('Bank RMSE (deg)');ax.set_title('Correcting joint energy does not resolve the turn mismatch');ax.legend();fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(O/'iteration-joint-energy-correction.png',dpi=150)
p=O/'physics-development.html';h=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');section='''<section id="joint-energy-audit"><h2>Finite-angle suspension spring correction</h2><p>The research joint used torque Kφ directly, where φ = log(RpᵀRc) is the relative rotation vector and K has unequal roll/pitch/yaw stiffnesses. For the intended potential U = ½φᵀKφ, the torque on the payload must instead be Rp J<sub>l</sub>(φ)<sup>−T</sup>Kφ, with equal and opposite torque on the canopy. J<sub>l</sub><sup>−1</sup> = I − ½[φ]× + [1/θ² − (1+cosθ)/(2θsinθ)][φ]×². The small-angle coefficient tends to 1/12. Relative-rate damping remains dissipative.</p><p>A 100-orientation finite-difference test (relative angle up to 1.3 rad) found maximum torque-gradient discrepancy 0.224 N·m for the old expression and 1.13×10<sup>−10</sup> N·m for the correction. This checks the spring expression against its chosen energy; it does not establish that this spring represents the real suspension geometry.</p><img src="iteration-joint-energy-correction.png" alt="Bank prediction errors before and after correcting the joint spring energy gradient" style="max-width:100%"><p>With coefficients frozen and the corrected propulsion diagnostic input, bank errors remain 5–22°. The spring correction is mechanically justified, but does not explain the sustained-turn mismatch. It is implemented in a separate research solver, with the historical solver retained for comparison. The flight replay remains conditional on measured RPM/inflow.</p></section>'''
if 'id="joint-energy-audit"' not in h:
 h=h.replace('</body>',section+'\n</body>') if '</body>' in h else h.replace('</html>',section+'\n</html>');p.write_text(h,encoding='utf-8')
